{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\"\n       xmlns:event=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event\"\n       version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"order\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"quantity\" expr=\"1\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"order\">\n    <onentry>\n      <send event=\"order.placed\"\n            event:schema='{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"quantity\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"quantity\"]}'>\n        <param name=\"quantity\" expr=\"quantity\"/>\n      </send>\n      <send event=\"order.note\"><content>{\"note\": 7}</content></send>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"order.placed\"\n                event:schema='{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"quantity\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"quantity\"]}'\n                target=\"done\"/>\n    <transition event=\"order.note\"\n                event:schema='{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"note\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}}'/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/event010-incompatible-event-data.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":2},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/event010-incompatible-event-data.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":114,"endLine":10,"startColumn":13,"startLine":10}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<send>` creates `order.placed` data that a transition handling it does not accept\n\n**Note:** a transition's `event:schema` describes the `_event.data` it handles; this data matches its event descriptor but not its schema (the schemas are metadata: the transition is still taken)\n\n**Help:** make the two schemas agree, or change the data\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.12.1 Event Descriptors","text":"`<send>` creates `order.placed` data that a transition handling it does not accept"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":432,"start":331},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"... fails the schema of this transition"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/event010-incompatible-event-data.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":117,"endLine":16,"startColumn":17,"startLine":16}}}],"ruleId":"EVENT010"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/event010-incompatible-event-data.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":62,"endLine":13,"startColumn":32,"startLine":13}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<send>` creates `order.note` data that a transition handling it does not accept\n\n**Note:** a transition's `event:schema` describes the `_event.data` it handles; this data matches its event descriptor but not its schema (the schemas are metadata: the transition is still taken)\n\n**Help:** make the two schemas agree, or change the data\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.12.1 Event Descriptors","text":"`<send>` creates `order.note` data that a transition handling it does not accept"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":558,"start":528},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"... fails the schema of this transition"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/event010-incompatible-event-data.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":89,"endLine":19,"startColumn":17,"startLine":19}}}],"ruleId":"EVENT010"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"in an ECMAScript document, a `<send event=\"x\">` delivered to its own session (no `target` or `#_internal`, the SCXML Event I/O Processor) or the `<donedata>` of a compound state (its `done.state.<id>`) creates data that a transition handling the event (SCXML 3.12.1 descriptor matching) describes with a literal `event:schema`; this is reported only when provable: the literal `<content>` data fails the transition's schema, or the producer's own literal schema admits an instance the transition's rejects (a witness drawn from its `const`, `enum`, `examples`, `default`, or a minimal instance of each `type`). Equal schemas and undecided cases are never reported; `event:schemaexpr` is skipped. The schemas are metadata, so the transition is still taken"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: make the two schemas agree, or change the data.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.12.1 Event Descriptors\n\nRun `scx --explain EVENT010` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#EventDescriptors","id":"EVENT010","name":"EVENT010","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a `<send>` or `<donedata>` creates event data a transition handling it does not accept"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}